  "body": "## What changed\n\nGit for Windows checks out text files with CRLF (`\\r\\n`) by default when `core.autocrlf=true`.\nPin test fixtures and golden output paths to LF line endings (`text eol=lf`) in `.gitattributes`:\n- Post output golden files and recorded streams (`crates/*/tests/golden/**`, `crates/*/tests/recorded/**`, `crates/*/tests/fixtures/**`)\n- Machine configuration files (`crates/*/tests/**/*.mch`, `assets/machines/**/*.mch`)\n- STEP, STL, and OBJ model fixtures (`testdata/**/*.step`, `testdata/**/*.stp`, `testdata/**/*.stl`, `testdata/**/*.obj`)\n- Skill, agent, and GitHub workflow definitions (`.claude/**`, `.github/**`)\n\nRenormalize line endings for `testdata/models/fig8.step`.\n\n## Readings and Pinning Tests\n\n- `xtask/tests/example_line_endings.rs:all_golden_and_fixture_files_have_eol_lf`: asserts `git check-attr eol` reports `lf` across all fixture, model, and workflow paths.\n- `xtask/tests/example_line_endings.rs:golden_and_fixture_files_keep_lf_with_autocrlf`: asserts checked-out fixture files contain no carriage returns under `core.autocrlf=true`.\n- Verified affected test suites pass: `explain_fanuc_family`, `wire_taper_angle`, `import_step_curve_guard`, and `post_merge_concurrency`.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- Non-Windows systems were not exercised locally (covered by CI).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nfork synced at v0.24.0\n\nFixes #2840\n",
